User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Expression limits depend on the pinned JSONata patch, but the distributed-image job only checked templates. The job now evaluates finite expressions through the compiled `@graphgoblin/domain` installed in the production image. The licence ledger documents what the patch provides and what to recheck when upgrading JSONata.\n\nThe new step checks ordinary evaluation, 250 siblings in an array and object, exact depth and deadline errors, and a successful evaluation after both refusals. It uses restrictive limits only for the two refusal probes. The existing image build and template checks remain in place.\n\nIndependent review ran the exact probe JavaScript against the compiled host package and all assertions passed. The author reported 29 passing domain expression tests and seven cached API build tasks. Scoped formatting and the diff check passed. The review’s one licence-wording correction was applied.\n\nThe hosted job still needs to verify the production image with networking disabled and a read-only root filesystem. The local result only establishes the host’s compiled package behavior. Timestamp isolation remains covered by the existing domain unit regression. Fresh independent Claude QA, required CI and final independent review are pending.\n\nThe [QA packet](docs/qa/2026-11-24-jsonata-package-467/README.md) binds the exact source and preserves the raw host execution and review records.\n\nCloses #467","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T02:04:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T03:50:35Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ad2bab47f4d9d70a63737bb10e8b6083cb905cff","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Jacob-J-Thomas:codex/gg-fu-jsonata-package-20261124","ref":"codex/gg-fu-jsonata-package-20261124","repo":{"id":1403707890,"node_id":"R_kgDOU6rh8g","name":"GraphGoblin","full_name":"Jacob-J-Thoma